WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.064
How does Catan Lens decide?

00:00:02.344 --> 00:00:08.253
It scores every legal corner with a few rules that strong players agree on, and production comes first.

00:00:08.884 --> 00:00:10.548
Each number token has dots.

00:00:10.828 --> 00:00:14.007
A six or an eight has five, a two or a twelve has one.

00:00:14.287 --> 00:00:18.404
The dots count the ways two dice can roll that number, out of thirty-six.

00:00:19.041 --> 00:00:23.692
A corner collects from up to three hexes, so its production is the sum of their dots.

00:00:23.972 --> 00:00:28.196
Wheat and ore count a little more, because they build cities and development cards.

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:32.375
A resource that is rare on this particular board is worth more.

00:00:32.655 --> 00:00:38.095
Smaller bonuses go to wood with brick, wheat with ore, a harbour you can feed, and room to grow.

00:00:38.375 --> 00:00:40.082
Repeating a number costs a little.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:49.104
Every rule traces back to a published source: expert guides, champion interviews, and a statistical study of four hundred online games.

00:00:49.742 --> 00:00:51.385
Placement is a snake draft.

00:00:51.665 --> 00:00:58.193
Projected placements plays it out for every seat, so you can see what will probably be gone before your turn comes back.

00:00:58.473 --> 00:01:02.995
The suggested road avoids corners other players are likely to take first.

00:01:03.637 --> 00:01:05.664
Drill mode turns this into practice.

00:01:05.944 --> 00:01:10.168
Set the table first: how many players, and whether you play Cities and Knights.

00:01:10.448 --> 00:01:14.885
Then climb sixteen levels, easy to hard, with hints hidden until you commit.

00:01:15.519 --> 00:01:20.554
Miss, and you see your rank and what the level needed, then get a fresh board at the same level.

00:01:21.185 --> 00:01:23.617
Hit the best corner, and the level is cleared.

00:01:23.897 --> 00:01:30.318
Later levels demand the exact best corner on near-ties, from any seat, and for your second settlement too.

00:01:30.952 --> 00:01:32.360
Playing at a real table?

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.240
Your board lets you copy it.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:41.112
Pick a resource and tap hexes to paint them, choose Numbers to set tokens, and tap the coast to place harbours.

00:01:42.511 --> 00:01:48.484
Every ranking then applies to your board, and Copy link saves the whole thing so you can share it with your table.

00:01:49.118 --> 00:01:50.846
Does the advice actually win?

00:01:51.126 --> 00:02:03.478
In thousands of simulated games between strong bots, openings chosen by Catan Lens won about as often as the bots' own searched openings, and far more often than just grabbing the most dots.
